# Enforce LF for every text file in the working tree on every platform.
# `core.autocrlf=true` on Windows otherwise rewrites chezmoi-source dotfiles
# with CRLF on checkout, which breaks them under WSL/zsh (e.g. `^M` errors)
# and tricks the run_after sync hook into spurious backups.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Known binaries — never normalize.
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.png binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary

# The absorbed service tree. These .ps1 are run standalone — possibly by Windows
# PowerShell 5.1, which reads a BOM-less file as ANSI and then dies on the
# non-ASCII characters they print — so they are UTF-8-WITH-BOM and CRLF by rule
# (docs/service-conventions.md). The global eol=lf above exists for the CHEZMOI
# SOURCE TREE and the sync hook; services/** is chezmoi-ignored and is not a
# sync root, so neither reason reaches here. This repo's own .ps1 files ARE
# synced and ARE run by pwsh 7, so they stay LF and BOM-less.
services/**/*.ps1 text eol=crlf
